  "id": "iwami_kagura",
  "name": "Iwami kagura (western Shimane kagura)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Iwami kagura is the kagura of the old Iwami province in western Shimane, played by local troupes (shachū) at autumn shrine festivals that run through the night, and it belongs to the Izumo type of kagura plays. Many troupes use the fast eight-beat hatchō-byōshi and stage spectacular myths such as the eight-headed serpent Orochi, to an ensemble of large drum, small drum, hand cymbals and transverse flute. The odaiko and shime-daiko cards stand in for the large and small drums and the kagurabue card for the flute.",
  "recipe": "classic modern iwami kagura, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. single lead single track no stacking. odaiko, shime daiko, credited cymbals, kagurabue. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
